{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786167260717,"sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_KVNxGCpmtm4csckVydTa0397","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deep Research Strategy: Pi Fork Improvements\n2: \n3: ## Research Topic\n4: \n5: Find concrete, evidence-based improvements for the vendored `pi-cache-optimizer` and `deep-pi` forks across correctness, test coverage, observability, cost economics, and maintainability.\n6: \n7: ## Known Context\n8: \n9: - The target spec has no `resource-map.md`; the coverage-map gate is informationally skipped.\n10: - `deep-pi` cannot expose the full `/deeppi report` body non-interactively, including RPC mode.\n11: - `deep-pi` has no persistent stats file comparable to `pi-cache-optimizer`.\n12: - A live regression check remains unresolved because the configured OpenCode credential was missing.\n13: - Cold-start cache writes for newly added models in `pi-cache-optimizer` are uncharacterized.\n14: \n15: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n16: ## Key Questions\n17: \n18: - [x] Which correctness and failure-isolation gaps remain in each fork?\n19: - [x] Which high-value boundary, fault-injection, and live-contract tests are missing?\n20: - [x] How should both forks expose durable, automation-friendly telemetry without leaking sensitive content?\n21: - [x] Which cost claims can be measured honestly, and what experiment design is needed?\n22: - [x] Which structural changes would reduce drift and maintenance burden without over-generalizing?\n23: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n24: \n25: ## Non-Goals\n26: \n27: - Do not implement fixes.\n28: - Do not modify either extension, sibling packet, or target spec.\n29: - Do not treat upstream claims as proven local behavior without local evidence.\n30: \n31: ## Stop Conditions\n32: \n33: - Complete exactly seven evidence iterations because the stop policy is `max-iterations`.\n34: - Produce a synthesis that ranks concrete improvements and records ruled-out directions and unresolved validation dependencies.\n35: \n36: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n37: ## Answered Questions\n38: \n39: - Correctness and failure-isolation gaps: iterations 1-2.\n40: - Boundary, fault-injection, and live-contract tests: iteration 3.\n41: - Automation-safe telemetry: iteration 4.\n42: - Honest cost claims and benchmark design: iteration 5.\n43: - Maintainability, provenance, and modularization: iteration 6.\n44: - Evidence-weighted implementation order and explicit deferrals: iteration 7.\n45: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n46: \n47: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n48: ## What Worked\n49: \n50: - Source-to-spec triangulation established the ownership baseline (iteration 1).\n51: - Transaction-level persistence tracing exposed cross-process and corruption failure modes (iteration 2).\n52: - Responsibility-to-test mapping exposed the missing DeepPi live benchmark and concrete cache-optimizer blind spots (iteration 3).\n53: - Separating structured data, text rendering, and transport produced an automation-safe telemetry design (iteration 4).\n54: - Provider-semantics comparison separated valid accounting from causal savings claims (iteration 5).\n55: - Package and export-boundary analysis exposed low-coupling stewardship controls (iteration 6).\n56: - Adversarial ranking separated demonstrated data loss from plausible but unobserved concurrency risk (iteration 7).\n57: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n58: \n59: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n60: ## What Failed\n61: \n62: - Broad grep over the monolithic cache optimizer was noisy; use named-function slices.\n63: - Static test counts differ from historical run totals and cannot serve as coverage evidence.\n64: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n65: \n66: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n67: ## Exhausted Approaches\n68: \n69: - Additional RPC transport probing before structured snapshot production.\n70: - One-score prioritization that obscures proof strength and dependency order.\n71: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n72: \n73: <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n74: ## Ruled-Out Directions\n75: \n76: - Broad DeepSeek matching as the ownership boundary: excludes non-direct routes incorrectly.\n77: - Atomic rename as a substitute for transaction-level concurrency control: prevents partial files, not lost updates.\n78: - Real credentials as the only boundary-regression proof: keep them as optional live confirmation over deterministic local integration tests.\n79: - Footer-only cold-start measurement: inspect structured counters across first, second, and restarted requests.\n80: - UI/RPC notifications as the canonical automation channel: persist versioned numeric snapshots instead.\n81: - Content-bearing or cross-extension shared telemetry state: retain separate, privacy-bounded files.\n82: - Single-pair cold/warm benchmarks and hard-coded live prices: use repeated crossover runs with price provenance.\n83: - Shared runtime ownership modules and one-shot rewrites: prefer fixtures, characterization tests, and staged extraction.\n84: - Locking DeepPi edits before reproducing concurrent-writer clobber: monitor and test first.\n85: <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n86: \n87: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n88: ## Next Focus\n89: \n90: [Synthesis complete; all tracked questions resolved]\n91: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n92: \n93: ## Research Boundaries\n94: \n95: - Maximum iterations: 7\n96: - Convergence threshold: 0.05 (telemetry only before iteration 7)\n97: - Allowed writes: this lineage directory only\n\n(End of file - total 97 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Deep Research Strategy: Pi Fork Improvements\n\n## Research Topic\n\nFind concrete, evidence-based improvements for the vendored `pi-cache-optimizer` and `deep-pi` forks across correctness, test coverage, observability, cost economics, and maintainability.\n\n## Known Context\n\n- The target spec has no `resource-map.md`; the coverage-map gate is informationally skipped.\n- `deep-pi` cannot expose the full `/deeppi report` body non-interactively, including RPC mode.\n- `deep-pi` has no persistent stats file comparable to `pi-cache-optimizer`.\n- A live regression check remains unresolved because the configured OpenCode credential was missing.\n- Cold-start cache writes for newly added models in `pi-cache-optimizer` are uncharacterized.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## Key Questions\n\n- [x] Which correctness and failure-isolation gaps remain in each fork?\n- [x] Which high-value boundary, fault-injection, and live-contract tests are missing?\n- [x] How should both forks expose durable, automation-friendly telemetry without leaking sensitive content?","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","text":"# Deep Research Strategy: Pi Fork Improvements\n\n## Research Topic\n\nFind concrete, evidence-based improvements for the vendored `pi-cache-optimizer` and `deep-pi` forks across correctness, test coverage, observability, cost economics, and maintainability.\n\n## Known Context\n\n- The target spec has no `resource-map.md`; the coverage-map gate is informationally skipped.\n- `deep-pi` cannot expose the full `/deeppi report` body non-interactively, including RPC mode.\n- `deep-pi` has no persistent stats file comparable to `pi-cache-optimizer`.\n- A live regression check remains unresolved because the configured OpenCode credential was missing.\n- Cold-start cache writes for newly added models in `pi-cache-optimizer` are uncharacterized.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## Key Questions\n\n- [x] Which correctness and failure-isolation gaps remain in each fork?\n- [x] Which high-value boundary, fault-injection, and live-contract tests are missing?\n- [x] How should both forks expose durable, automation-friendly telemetry without leaking sensitive content?\n- [x] Which cost claims can be measured honestly, and what experiment design is needed?\n- [x] Which structural changes would reduce drift and maintenance burden without over-generalizing?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n## Non-Goals\n\n- Do not implement fixes.\n- Do not modify either extension, sibling packet, or target spec.\n- Do not treat upstream claims as proven local behavior without local evidence.\n\n## Stop Conditions\n\n- Complete exactly seven evidence iterations because the stop policy is `max-iterations`.\n- Produce a synthesis that ranks concrete improvements and records ruled-out directions and unresolved validation dependencies.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## Answered Questions\n\n- Correctness and failure-isolation gaps: iterations 1-2.\n- Boundary, fault-injection, and live-contract tests: iteration 3.\n- Automation-safe telemetry: iteration 4.\n- Honest cost claims and benchmark design: iteration 5.\n- Maintainability, provenance, and modularization: iteration 6.\n- Evidence-weighted implementation order and explicit deferrals: iteration 7.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## What Worked\n\n- Source-to-spec triangulation established the ownership baseline (iteration 1).\n- Transaction-level persistence tracing exposed cross-process and corruption failure modes (iteration 2).\n- Responsibility-to-test mapping exposed the missing DeepPi live benchmark and concrete cache-optimizer blind spots (iteration 3).\n- Separating structured data, text rendering, and transport produced an automation-safe telemetry design (iteration 4).\n- Provider-semantics comparison separated valid accounting from causal savings claims (iteration 5).\n- Package and export-boundary analysis exposed low-coupling stewardship controls (iteration 6).\n- Adversarial ranking separated demonstrated data loss from plausible but unobserved concurrency risk (iteration 7).\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## What Failed\n\n- Broad grep over the monolithic cache optimizer was noisy; use named-function slices.\n- Static test counts differ from historical run totals and cannot serve as coverage evidence.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## Exhausted Approaches\n\n- Additional RPC transport probing before structured snapshot production.\n- One-score prioritization that obscures proof strength and dependency order.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## Ruled-Out Directions\n\n- Broad DeepSeek matching as the ownership boundary: excludes non-direct routes incorrectly.\n- Atomic rename as a substitute for transaction-level concurrency control: prevents partial files, not lost updates.\n- Real credentials as the only boundary-regression proof: keep them as optional live confirmation over deterministic local integration tests.\n- Footer-only cold-start measurement: inspect structured counters across first, second, and restarted requests.\n- UI/RPC notifications as the canonical automation channel: persist versioned numeric snapshots instead.\n- Content-bearing or cross-extension shared telemetry state: retain separate, privacy-bounded files.\n- Single-pair cold/warm benchmarks and hard-coded live prices: use repeated crossover runs with price provenance.\n- Shared runtime ownership modules and one-shot rewrites: prefer fixtures, characterization tests, and staged extraction.\n- Locking DeepPi edits before reproducing concurrent-writer clobber: monitor and test first.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## Next Focus\n\n[Synthesis complete; all tracked questions resolved]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n## Research Boundaries\n\n- Maximum iterations: 7\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05 (telemetry only before iteration 7)\n- Allowed writes: this lineage directory only","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":97,"totalLines":97,"truncated":false}},"title":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","time":{"start":1786167260710,"end":1786167260716}},"id":"prt_fdfdd74b3001jKRbl4kYUXlGT4","sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","messageID":"msg_fdfdd63530013DR8277eNoiz1h"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786167261276,"sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_a400lKeN2kWwpdOWFxCk3113","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\"type\":\"config\",\"topic\":\"How to further improve the two forked Pi extensions built in packet 039: pi-cache-optimizer's DeepSeek-guard fork and deep-pi's hardened DeepSeek-direct fork, covering correctness, test coverage, telemetry/observability, cost-economics, and maintainability\",\"maxIterations\":7,\"minIterations\":3,\"convergenceThreshold\":0.05,\"antiConvergence\":{\"convergenceMode\":\"default\",\"stopPolicy\":\"max-iterations\"},\"minIdeaObservations\":2,\"resource_map_present\":false,\"resource_map\":{\"emit\":true},\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-08T04:30:50Z\",\"specFolder\":\"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-sol-1786163355542-f6htbk\",\"generation\":1,\"nextRunAt\":null,\"remainingDelayMs\":null}\n2: {\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":1,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Baseline architecture and ownership contract\",\"findingsCount\":5,\"newInfoRatio\":1.0,\"noveltyJustification\":\"First lineage pass; all five synthesized baseline findings are new to this packet.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which correctness and failure-isolation gaps remain in each fork?\",\"How should both forks expose durable, automation-friendly telemetry without leaking sensitive content?\",\"Which structural changes would reduce drift and maintenance burden without over-generalizing?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[],\"ruledOut\":[\"Use the broad DeepSeek-like predicate as the ownership boundary\",\"Activate deep-pi for every future deepseek-v model id without widening its state model\"],\"focusTrack\":\"architecture\",\"edgeCase\":\"none\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/eligibility.ts\",\"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/003-fork-and-guard-cache-optimizer/implementation-summary.md\",\"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/006-fork-and-improve-deep-pi/001-fix-and-test-deep-pi/spec.md\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-08T04:31:58Z\",\"durationMs\":68000,\"keyFindings\":[{\"id\":\"f-ownership-contract-drift\",\"summary\":\"The DeepPi ownership predicate is duplicated across both forks and can drift.\"},{\"id\":\"f-report-ui-only\",\"summary\":\"DeepPi's full report is coupled to ctx.ui.notify.\"},{\"id\":\"f-state-asymmetry\",\"summary\":\"Only pi-cache-optimizer persists cross-session cache economics.\"},{\"id\":\"f-monolith\",\"summary\":\"pi-cache-optimizer concentrates 8,390 lines in one source file.\"},{\"id\":\"f-guard-proven\",\"summary\":\"The six-hook exclusion guard is already liv... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n3: {\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":2,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":2,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Persistence and concurrency correctness\",\"findingsCount\":5,\"newInfoRatio\":0.9,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Four of five findings are new; one partly extends the known atomic-write hardening evidence.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which correctness and failure-isolation gaps remain in each fork?\",\"Which high-value boundary, fault-injection, and live-contract tests are missing?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Which correctness and failure-isolation gaps remain in each fork?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Atomic rename alone is sufficient concurrency control\",\"Add a permanent sidecar lock without stale-owner recovery\"],\"focusTrack\":\"correctness\",\"edgeCase\":\"contradictory-evidence\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4215\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4264\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts:58\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/tests/review2.test.ts:50\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-08T04:33:03Z\",\"durationMs\":65000,\"keyFindings\":[{\"id\":\"f-pco-cross-process-lost-update\",\"summary\":\"pi-cache-optimizer's shared stats read/merge/rename transaction has no cross-process concurrency control.\"},{\"id\":\"f-pco-corrupt-overwrite\",\"summary\":\"Malformed persisted stats are silently treated as empty and can be overwritten.\"},{\"id\":\"f-pco-temp-hygiene\",\"summary\":\"Persistence temp files use collision-prone names and lack guaranteed cleanup.\"},{\"id\":\"f-deeppi-cas-gap\",\"summary\":\"edit_lines still has a cross-process TOCTOU window between expected-content check and rename.\"},{\"id\":\"f-persistence-test-gap\",\"summary\":\"pi-cache-optimizer lacks direct persistence fault and race tests.\"}],\"graphEvents\":[]}\n4: {\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":3,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":3,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Test coverage and executable evidence gaps\",\"findingsCount\":5,\"newInfoRatio\":0.9,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Four findings are fully new and the credential strategy materially reframes a known limitation.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which high-value boundary, fault-injection, and live-contract tests are missing?\",\"Which cost claims can be measured honestly, and what experiment design is needed?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Which high-value boundary, fault-injection, and live-contract tests are missing?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Use raw test count as coverage evidence\",\"Require real credentials for every boundary regression\",\"Use footer output alone for cold-start cache-write characterization\"],\"focusTrack\":\"testing\",\"edgeCase\":\"partial-success\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/README.md\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/tests/package.test.ts\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/tests/review-findings.test.ts\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:3645\",\"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/006-fork-and-improve-deep-pi/003-live-verification-and-closeout/tasks.md:60\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-08T04:34:33Z\",\"durationMs\":90000,\"keyFindings\":[{\"id\":\"f-deeppi-broken-live-benchmark\",\"summary\":\"DeepPi's documented benchmark command points to a missing, unpackaged script.\"},{\"id\":\"f-pco-runtime-test-blindspots\",\"summary\":\"Cache optimizer tests omit direct persistence, adapter-matrix, and message_end state coverage.\"},{\"id\":\"f-cold-start-test-design\",\"summary\":\"Cold-start characterization requires structured first/second/restart measurements, not footer-only inspection.\"},{\"id\":\"f-credential-independent-boundary-test\",\"summary\":\"A local Pi/provider fixture can prove routing boundaries w... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n5: {\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":4,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":4,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Telemetry and non-interactive observability\",\"findingsCount\":5,\"newInfoRatio\":0.8,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Three findings are new designs and two consolidate prior gaps into a coherent observability contract.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"How should both forks expose durable, automation-friendly telemetry without leaking sensitive content?\",\"Which structural changes would reduce drift and maintenance burden without over-generalizing?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"How should both forks expose durable, automation-friendly telemetry without leaking sensitive content?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Use RPC notifications as the canonical report transport\",\"Persist content-bearing telemetry\",\"Use one shared writable state file for both extensions\"],\"focusTrack\":\"observability\",\"edgeCase\":\"contradictory-evidence\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts:64\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/telemetry.ts:80\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:330\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:370\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:7025\",\"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/006-fork-and-improve-deep-pi/003-live-verification-and-closeout/implementation-summary.md:60\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-08T04:35:54Z\",\"durationMs\":81000,\"keyFindings\":[{\"id\":\"f-deeppi-versioned-snapshot\",\"summary\":\"DeepPi should atomically persist a versioned structured report used by both TUI and automation.\"},{\"id\":\"f-deeppi-dual-scope-stats\",\"summary\":\"DeepPi needs current-session and daily cumulative telemetry scopes.\"},{\"id\":\"f-pco-durable-health-aggregates\",\"summary\":\"Cache optimizer should persist bounded health aggregates instead of raw per-request samples.\"},{\"id\":\"f-report-data-render-transport\",\"summary\"... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n6: {\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":5,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":5,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Cost economics and benchmark design\",\"findingsCount\":5,\"newInfoRatio\":0.85,\"noveltyJustification\":\"The pass distinguishes valid accounting from causal claims and turns four known limitations into one controlled experiment.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which cost claims can be measured honestly, and what experiment design is needed?\",\"Which structural changes would reduce drift and maintenance burden without over-generalizing?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Which cost claims can be measured honestly, and what experiment design is needed?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Call estimated savings a measured extension benefit\",\"Use a single cold/warm request pair\",\"Freeze provider prices in source tests\"],\"focusTrack\":\"cost-economics\",\"edgeCase\":\"contradictory-evidence\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Web\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/telemetry.ts:47\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:3645\",\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/kv_cache\",\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/api/create-completion\",\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-08T04:38:12Z\",\"durationMs\":138000,\"keyFindings\":[{\"id\":\"f-savings-counterfactual-label\",\"summary\":\"DeepPi's savings arithmetic is a no-cache counterfactual, not causal extension savings.\"},{\"id\":\"f-cache-write-accounting\",\"summary\":\"DeepPi silently omits nonzero cache-write usage and should surface the model-specific assumption.\"},{\"id\":\"f-price-provenance\",\"summary\":\"Benchmark outputs need timestamped model-price provenance rather than hard-coded current rates.\"},{\"id\":\"f-crossover-benchmark\",\"summary\":\"Cold/warm economics require repeated randomized enabled/disable