e six-hook exclusion guard is already liv... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":2,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":2,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Persistence and concurrency correctness\",\"findingsCount\":5,\"newInfoRatio\":0.9,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Four of five findings are new; one partly extends the known atomic-write hardening evidence.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which correctness and failure-isolation gaps remain in each fork?\",\"Which high-value boundary, fault-injection, and live-contract tests are missing?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Which correctness and failure-isolation gaps remain in each fork?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Atomic rename alone is sufficient concurrency control\",\"Add a permanent sidecar lock without stale-owner recovery\"],\"focusTrack\":\"correctness\",\"edgeCase\":\"contradictory-evidence\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4215\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4264\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts:58\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/tests/review2.test.ts:50\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-08T04:33:03Z\",\"durationMs\":65000,\"keyFindings\":[{\"id\":\"f-pco-cross-process-lost-update\",\"summary\":\"pi-cache-optimizer's shared stats read/merge/rename transaction has no cross-process concurrency control.\"},{\"id\":\"f-pco-corrupt-overwrite\",\"summary\":\"Malformed persisted stats are silently treated as empty and can be overwritten.\"},{\"id\":\"f-pco-temp-hygiene\",\"summary\":\"Persistence temp files use collision-prone names and lack guaranteed cleanup.\"},{\"id\":\"f-deeppi-cas-gap\",\"summary\":\"edit_lines still has a cross-process TOCTOU window between expected-content check and rename.\"},{\"id\":\"f-persistence-test-gap\",\"summary\":\"pi-cache-optimizer lacks direct persistence fault and race tests.\"}],\"graphEvents\":[]}\n{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":3,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":3,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Test coverage and executable evidence gaps\",\"findingsCount\":5,\"newInfoRatio\":0.9,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Four findings are fully new and the credential strategy materially reframes a known limitation.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which high-value boundary, fault-injection, and live-contract tests are missing?\",\"Which cost claims can be measured honestly, and what experiment design is needed?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Which high-value boundary, fault-injection, and live-contract tests are missing?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Use raw test count as coverage evidence\",\"Require real credentials for every boundary regression\",\"Use footer output alone for cold-start cache-write characterization\"],\"focusTrack\":\"testing\",\"edgeCase\":\"partial-success\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/README.md\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/tests/package.test.ts\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/tests/review-findings.test.ts\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:3645\",\"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/006-fork-and-improve-deep-pi/003-live-verification-and-closeout/tasks.md:60\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-08T04:34:33Z\",\"durationMs\":90000,\"keyFindings\":[{\"id\":\"f-deeppi-broken-live-benchmark\",\"summary\":\"DeepPi's documented benchmark command points to a missing, unpackaged script.\"},{\"id\":\"f-pco-runtime-test-blindspots\",\"summary\":\"Cache optimizer tests omit direct persistence, adapter-matrix, and message_end state coverage.\"},{\"id\":\"f-cold-start-test-design\",\"summary\":\"Cold-start characterization requires structured first/second/restart measurements, not footer-only inspection.\"},{\"id\":\"f-credential-independent-boundary-test\",\"summary\":\"A local Pi/provider fixture can prove routing boundaries w... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":4,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":4,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Telemetry and non-interactive observability\",\"findingsCount\":5,\"newInfoRatio\":0.8,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Three findings are new designs and two consolidate prior gaps into a coherent observability contract.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"How should both forks expose durable, automation-friendly telemetry without leaking sensitive content?\",\"Which structural changes would reduce drift and maintenance burden without over-generalizing?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"How should both forks expose durable, automation-friendly telemetry without leaking sensitive content?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Use RPC notifications as the canonical report transport\",\"Persist content-bearing telemetry\",\"Use one shared writable state file for both extensions\"],\"focusTrack\":\"observability\",\"edgeCase\":\"contradictory-evidence\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts:64\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/telemetry.ts:80\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:330\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:370\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:7025\",\"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/006-fork-and-improve-deep-pi/003-live-verification-and-closeout/implementation-summary.md:60\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-08T04:35:54Z\",\"durationMs\":81000,\"keyFindings\":[{\"id\":\"f-deeppi-versioned-snapshot\",\"summary\":\"DeepPi should atomically persist a versioned structured report used by both TUI and automation.\"},{\"id\":\"f-deeppi-dual-scope-stats\",\"summary\":\"DeepPi needs current-session and daily cumulative telemetry scopes.\"},{\"id\":\"f-pco-durable-health-aggregates\",\"summary\":\"Cache optimizer should persist bounded health aggregates instead of raw per-request samples.\"},{\"id\":\"f-report-data-render-transport\",\"summary\"... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":5,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":5,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Cost economics and benchmark design\",\"findingsCount\":5,\"newInfoRatio\":0.85,\"noveltyJustification\":\"The pass distinguishes valid accounting from causal claims and turns four known limitations into one controlled experiment.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which cost claims can be measured honestly, and what experiment design is needed?\",\"Which structural changes would reduce drift and maintenance burden without over-generalizing?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Which cost claims can be measured honestly, and what experiment design is needed?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Call estimated savings a measured extension benefit\",\"Use a single cold/warm request pair\",\"Freeze provider prices in source tests\"],\"focusTrack\":\"cost-economics\",\"edgeCase\":\"contradictory-evidence\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Web\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/telemetry.ts:47\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:3645\",\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/kv_cache\",\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/api/create-completion\",\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-08T04:38:12Z\",\"durationMs\":138000,\"keyFindings\":[{\"id\":\"f-savings-counterfactual-label\",\"summary\":\"DeepPi's savings arithmetic is a no-cache counterfactual, not causal extension savings.\"},{\"id\":\"f-cache-write-accounting\",\"summary\":\"DeepPi silently omits nonzero cache-write usage and should surface the model-specific assumption.\"},{\"id\":\"f-price-provenance\",\"summary\":\"Benchmark outputs need timestamped model-price provenance rather than hard-coded current rates.\"},{\"id\":\"f-crossover-benchmark\",\"summary\":\"Cold/warm economics require repeated randomized enabled/disabled crossover measurements.\"},{\"id\":\"f-local-overhead-ablation\",\"summary\":\"Monotonic per-hook timing and feature ablations are... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":6,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":6,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Maintainability and fork stewardship\",\"findingsCount\":5,\"newInfoRatio\":0.75,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Four concrete stewardship mechanisms are new; the shared ownership drift is refined into a low-coupling test design.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which structural changes would reduce drift and maintenance burden without over-generalizing?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Which structural changes would reduce drift and maintenance burden without over-generalizing?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Create one shared production eligibility module\",\"Split the cache optimizer wholesale in one change\",\"Replace upstream history with a clean fork\"],\"focusTrack\":\"maintainability\",\"edgeCase\":\"partial-success\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/package.json:3\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:6471\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json:3\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts:165\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/eligibility.ts:1\",\"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/003-fork-and-guard-cache-optimizer/implementation-summary.md\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-08T04:40:06Z\",\"durationMs\":114000,\"keyFindings\":[{\"id\":\"f-fork-build-identity\",\"summary\":\"Both forks need unique build identity and local provenance instead of unchanged upstream metadata.\"},{\"id\":\"f-ownership-contract-fixture\",\"summary\":\"A shared fixture matrix can prevent predicate drift without runtime package coupling.\"},{\"id\":\"f-pco-staged-modularization\",\"summary\":\"Cache optimizer modularization should proceed by characterized responsibility seams.\"},{\"id\":\"f-deeppi-hygiene-gates\",\"summary\":\"Duplicate declarations and missing script packaging justify structural hygiene gates.\"},{\"id\":\"f-patch-ledger\",\"summary\":\"A machine-readable... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":7,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":7,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Adversarial prioritization\",\"findingsCount\":5,\"newInfoRatio\":0.45,\"noveltyJustification\":\"No new defect class was needed; the value is an evidence-weighted order and explicit deferrals.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which correctness and failure-isolation gaps remain in each fork?\",\"Which high-value boundary, fault-injection, and live-contract tests are missing?\",\"How should both forks expose durable, automation-friendly telemetry without leaking sensitive content?\",\"Which cost claims can be measured honestly, and what experiment design is needed?\",\"Which structural changes would reduce drift and maintenance burden without over-generalizing?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Which correctness and failure-isolation gaps remain in each fork?\",\"Which high-value boundary, fault-injection, and live-contract tests are missing?\",\"How should both forks expose durable, automation-friendly telemetry without leaking sensitive content?\",\"Which cost claims can be measured honestly, and what experiment design is needed?\",\"Which structural changes would reduce drift and maintenance burden without over-generalizing?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Start with monolith refactoring\",\"Treat every concurrency risk as equally urgent\",\"Continue RPC experiments before structured snapshots\"],\"focusTrack\":\"synthesis-prioritization\",\"edgeCase\":\"contradictory-evidence\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\",\"Web\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\"iterations/iteration-001.md\",\"iterations/iteration-002.md\",\"iterations/iteration-003.md\",\"iterations/iteration-004.md\",\"iterations/iteration-005.md\",\"iterations/iteration-006.md\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4264\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts:83\",\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/kv_cache\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-08T04:42:14Z\",\"durationMs\":128... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"synthesis_complete\",\"totalIterations\":7,\"answeredCount\":5,\"totalQuestions\":5,\"stopReason\":\"maxIterationsReached\",\"sourceFindings\":35,\"reconstructionGaps\":0,\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-08T04:44:10Z\"}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":9,"totalLines":9,"truncated":false}},"title":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl","time":{"start":1786167261268,"end":1786167261273}},"id":"prt_fdfdd76d60013Pz3TTLSYW4plH","sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","messageID":"msg_fdfdd63530013DR8277eNoiz1h"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1786167262616,"sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","part":{"id":"prt_fdfdd7d95001BmYcK6EBSzLSiV","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","messageID":"msg_fdfdd63530013DR8277eNoiz1h","sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":77346,"input":4523,"output":192,"reasoning":55,"cache":{"write":0,"read":72576}},"cost":0.0004527964}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1786167266815,"sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","part":{"id":"prt_fdfdd8dfa001Ts1AAue8EwSnUQ","messageID":"msg_fdfdd82b4001lC0GA1n6ifLj3o","sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786167269050,"sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_lVKwBDZkEPRihwGBMHHb7083","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Iteration 1: Baseline Architecture and Ownership Contract\n2: \n3: ## Focus\n4: \n5: Establish what each fork currently owns, what has already been proven, and which seams deserve deeper investigation rather than rediscovering closed work.\n6: \n7: ## Findings\n8: \n9: 1. The runtime ownership split is correct but duplicated: `deep-pi` declares the two direct DeepSeek ids in `DEEPPI_MODEL_IDS`, while `pi-cache-optimizer` independently repeats the same provider/id predicate. Any future supported-model change therefore requires a coordinated two-repository edit; a mismatch can create either double mutation or a coverage hole. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/eligibility.ts:1] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:1279]\n10: 2. `pi-cache-optimizer` guards all six model-specific hooks, and the completed packet has live evidence for direct DeepSeek silence plus continued coverage of non-direct DeepSeek-family and non-DeepSeek models. The remaining improvement is contract-level drift detection, not broader guard logic. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:7279] [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/003-fork-and-guard-cache-optimizer/implementation-summary.md:85]\n11: 3. `deep-pi` is intentionally modular (eligibility, stability, storm breaker, telemetry, hashlines), but its entry point still funnels its full report only through `ctx.ui.notify`; this explains why non-interactive report capture remains a product-interface gap rather than a telemetry-format gap. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts:1] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts:64]\n12: 4. The two projects have sharply asymmetric state lifecycles: `pi-cache-optimizer` advertises daily/session/process persisted stats and a persisted config, while `deep-pi` resets all telemetry at session start and has no durable storage path. This makes cross-session economics incomparable even though both claim cache economics. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:85] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts:46]\n13: 5. Maintenance risk is concentrated in `pi-cache-optimizer`'s 8,390-line single source file and 887-line single test file, whereas `deep-pi` has 1,341 source lines split across seven modules and 1,213 test lines split across eight files. This is objective structural debt: the cache optimizer combines parsing, persistence, UI, provider adapters, mutation hooks, repair, and diagnostics in one compilation unit. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:1] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/tests/review-findings.test.ts:1] [INFERENCE: line counts from `wc -l` over both vendored extension trees]\n14: \n15: ## Ruled Out\n16: \n17: - Reusing `pi-cache-optimizer`'s broad `isDeepSeekLikeModel` for ownership is unsafe because it intentionally matches non-direct DeepSeek-family routes that must stay cache-optimizer-owned. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:1275]\n18: - Re-activating `deep-pi` for every future `deepseek-v*` id remains unsafe until telemetry storage and model-specific assumptions become open-ended; the completed packet already traced the crash path. [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/006-fork-and-improve-deep-pi/001-fix-and-test-deep-pi/spec.md:79]\n19: \n20: ## Dead Ends\n21: \n22: - Treating the known non-interactive report limitation as proof that RPC exposes nothing. Prior live work confirmed RPC carries some extension UI events; the unresolved question is full-body delivery. [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/006-fork-and-improve-deep-pi/003-live-verification-and-closeout/implementation-summary.md:60]\n23: \n24: ## Edge Cases\n25: \n26: - Ambiguous input: none.\n27: - Contradictory evidence: none.\n28: - Missing dependencies: no target `resource-map.md`; direct source inventory substituted.\n29: - Partial success: none.\n30: \n31: ## Sources Consulted\n32: \n33: - `.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts`\n34: - `.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md`\n35: - `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts`\n36: - `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/eligibility.ts`\n37: - sibling packet 003 and 006 implementation summaries/specs\n38: \n39: ## Assessment\n40: \n41: - New information ratio: 1.0\n42: - Novelty justification: First lineage pass; all five synthesized baseline findings are new to this packet.\n43: - Questions addressed: correctness ownership, observability asymmetry, maintainability.\n44: - Questions answered: none fully; the baseline narrows subsequent investigation.\n45: \n46: ## Reflection\n47: \n48: - What worked and why: pairing source reads with sibling closeout evidence separated proven guarantees from remaining gaps.\n49: - What did not work and why: broad grep output was noisy because `index.ts` is unusually large; subsequent passes should target named functions and line ranges.\n50: - What I would do differently: audit one concern per pass with focused source slices and executable checks.\n51: \n52: ## Recommended Next Focus\n53: \n54: Audit correctness and failure isolation around state persistence, atomic writes, concurrent events, and the cross-extension ownership seam.\n\n(End of file - total 54 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Iteration 1: Baseline Architecture and Ownership Contract\n\n## Focus\n\nEstablish what each fork currently owns, what has already been proven, and which seams deserve deeper investigation rather than rediscovering closed work.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The runtime ownership split is correct but duplicated: `deep-pi` declares the two direct DeepSeek ids in `DEEPPI_MODEL_IDS`, while `pi-cache-optimizer` independently repeats the same provider/id predicate. Any future supported-model change therefore requires a coordinated two-repository edit; a mismatch can create either double mutation or a coverage hole. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/eligibility.ts:1] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:1279]\n2. `pi-cache-optimizer` guards all six model-specific hooks, and the completed packet has live evidence for direct DeepSeek silence plus continued coverage of non-direct DeepSeek-family and non-DeepSeek models. The remaining improvement is contract-level drift detection, not broader guard logic. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:7279] [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/003-fork-and-guard-cache-optimizer/implementation-summary.md:85]\n3. `deep-pi` is intentionally modular (eligibility, stability, storm breaker, telemetry, hashlines), but its entry point still funnels its full report only through `ctx.ui.notify`; this explains why non-interactive report capture remains a product-interface gap rather than a telemetry-format gap. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts:1] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts:64]\n4. The two projects have sharply asymmetric state lifecycles: `pi-cache-optimizer` advertises daily/session/process persisted stats and a persisted config, while `deep-pi` resets all telemetry at session start and has no durable storage path. This makes cross-session economics incomparable even though both claim cache economics. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:85] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts:46]\n5. Maintenance risk is concentrated in `pi-cache-optimizer`'s 8,390-line single source file and 887-line single test file, whereas `deep-pi` has 1,341 source lines split across seven modules and 1,213 test lines split across eight files. This is objective structural debt: the cache optimizer combines parsing, persistence, UI, provider adapters, mutation hooks, repair, and diagnostics in one compilation unit. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:1] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/tests/review-findings.test.ts:1] [INFERENCE: line counts from `wc -l` over both vendored extension trees]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Reusing `pi-cache-optimizer`'s broad `isDeepSeekLikeModel` for ownership is unsafe because it intentionally matches non-direct DeepSeek-family routes that must stay cache-optimizer-owned. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:1275]\n- Re-activating `deep-pi` for every future `deepseek-v*` id remains unsafe until telemetry storage and model-specific assumptions become open-ended; the completed packet already traced the crash path. [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/006-fork-and-improve-deep-pi/001-fix-and-test-deep-pi/spec.md:79]\n\n## Dead Ends","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md","text":"# Iteration 1: Baseline Architecture and Ownership Contract\n\n## Focus\n\nEstablish what each fork currently owns, what has already been proven, and which seams deserve deeper investigation rather than rediscovering closed work.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The runtime ownership split is correct but duplicated: `deep-pi` declares the two direct DeepSeek ids in `DEEPPI_MODEL_IDS`, while `pi-cache-optimizer` independently repeats the same provider/id predicate. Any future supported-model change therefore requires a coordinated two-repository edit; a mismatch can create either double mutation or a coverage hole. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/eligibility.ts:1] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:1279]\n2. `pi-cache-optimizer` guards all six model-specific hooks, and the completed packet has live evidence for direct DeepSeek silence plus continued coverage of non-direct DeepSeek-family and non-DeepSeek models. The remaining improvement is contract-level drift detection, not broader guard logic. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:7279] [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/003-fork-and-guard-cache-optimizer/implementation-summary.md:85]\n3. `deep-pi` is intentionally modular (eligibility, stability, storm breaker, telemetry, hashlines), but its entry point still funnels its full report only through `ctx.ui.notify`; this explains why non-interactive report capture remains a product-interface gap rather than a telemetry-format gap. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts:1] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts:64]\n4. The two projects have sharply asymmetric state lifecycles: `pi-cache-optimizer` advertises daily/session/process persisted stats and a persisted config, while `deep-pi` resets all telemetry at session start and has no durable storage path. This makes cross-session economics incomparable even though both claim cache economics. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:85] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts:46]\n5. Maintenance risk is concentrated in `pi-cache-optimizer`'s 8,390-line single source file and 887-line single test file, whereas `deep-pi` has 1,341 source lines split across seven modules and 1,213 test lines split across eight files. This is objective structural debt: the cache optimizer combines parsing, persistence, UI, provider adapters, mutation hooks, repair, and diagnostics in one compilation unit. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:1] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/tests/review-findings.test.ts:1] [INFERENCE: line counts from `wc -l` over both vendored extension trees]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Reusing `pi-cache-optimizer`'s broad `isDeepSeekLikeModel` for ownership is unsafe because it intentionally matches non-direct DeepSeek-family routes that must stay cache-optimizer-owned. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:1275]\n- Re-activating `deep-pi` for every future `deepseek-v*` id remains unsafe until telemetry storage and model-specific assumptions become open-ended; the completed packet already traced the crash path. [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/006-fork-and-improve-deep-pi/001-fix-and-test-deep-pi/spec.md:79]\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Treating the known non-interactive report limitation as proof that RPC exposes nothing. Prior live work confirmed RPC carries some extension UI events; the unresolved question is full-body delivery. [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/006-fork-and-improve-deep-pi/003-live-verification-and-closeout/implementation-summary.md:60]\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: none.\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\n- Missing dependencies: no target `resource-map.md`; direct source inventory substituted.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts`\n- `.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md`\n- `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts`\n- `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/eligibility.ts`\n- sibling packet 003 and 006 implementation summaries/specs\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 1.0\n- Novelty justification: First lineage pass; all five synthesized baseline findings are new to this packet.\n- Questions addressed: correctness ownership, observability asymmetry, maintainability.\n- Questions answered: none fully; the baseline narrows subsequent investigation.\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: pairing source reads with sibling closeout evidence separated proven guarantees from remaining gaps.\n- What did not work and why: broad grep output was noisy because `index.ts` is unusually large; subsequent passes should target named functions and line ranges.\n- What I would do differently: audit one concern per pass with focused source slices and executable checks.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nAudit correctness and failure isolation around state persistence, atomic writes, concurrent events, and the cross-extension ownership seam.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":54,"totalLines":54,"truncated":false}},"title":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md","time":{"start":1786167269034,"end":1786167269048}},"id":"prt_fdfdd9537001FT0wWVmMMCwnKs","sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","messageID":"msg_fdfdd82b4001lC0GA1n6ifLj3o"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786167269434,"sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_5XpeHlnl9McjtTqE5fbI6996","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-001.jsonl"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-001.jsonl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":1,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Baseline architecture and ownership contract\",\"findingsCount\":5,\"newInfoRatio\":1.0,\"noveltyJustification\":\"First lineage pass; all five synthesized baseline findings are new to this packet.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which correctness and failure-isolation gaps remain in each fork?\",\"How should both forks expose durable, automation-friendly telemetry without leaking sensitive content?\",\"Which structural changes would reduce drift and maintenance burden without over-generalizing?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[],\"ruledOut\":[\"Use the broad DeepSeek-like predicate as the ownership boundary\",\"Activate deep-pi for every future deepseek-v model id without widening its state model\"],\"focusTrack\":\"architecture\",\"edgeCase\":\"none\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts\",\".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts\",\".pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/eligibility.ts\",\"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-cac