{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1786167703221,"sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","part":{"id":"prt_fdfe436b1001VMhE558C2bnoGY","messageID":"msg_fdfe42a20001xkMbv3MJIzS2fF","sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786167704375,"sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_ET_FRcNLmYtqnj86UOT3TiT2256","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.pi/extensions/deep-pi/README.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.pi/extensions/deep-pi/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # DeepPi\n2: \n3: Reasonix-style DeepSeek price/performance for the Pi coding agent.\n4: \n5: DeepPi targets the direct DeepSeek API only. It stabilizes cacheable request\n6: prefixes, reports measured cache economics from Pi's real usage records, and\n7: reduces paid retries with loop guards and hash-verified edits.\n8: \n9: ## Supported models\n10: \n11: - `deepseek-v4-flash`\n12: - `deepseek-v4-pro`\n13: \n14: DeepPi is dormant for every other provider and model.\n15: \n16: ## Install\n17: \n18: ```bash\n19: pi install git:github.com/christopherarter/deep-pi\n20: ```\n21: \n22: Reload Pi, select a supported direct DeepSeek model, and run `/deeppi`.\n23: \n24: ## What `/deeppi` measures\n25: \n26: - cache-read and uncached input tokens;\n27: - cache-hit rate;\n28: - actual input cost from Pi;\n29: - estimated savings against fully uncached input;\n30: - detected local prefix churn;\n31: - guarded retry loops and hashline edit outcomes.\n32: \n33: DeepPi does not promise a fixed hit rate. Provider cache expiry and backend\n34: state can produce misses even when the local request prefix is stable.\n35: \n36: ## Development\n37: \n38: ```bash\n39: npm install --ignore-scripts\n40: npm run verify\n41: ```\n42: \n43: Default verification never calls an external API. The paid smoke benchmark is\n44: explicitly opt-in:\n45: \n46: ```bash\n47: DEEPPI_LIVE=1 npm run benchmark:live\n48: ```\n49: \n50: ## Attribution\n51: \n52: DeepPi is derived from\n53: [`jrimmer/pi-deepseek-optimized`](https://github.com/jrimmer/pi-deepseek-optimized)\n54: and is licensed under the Apache License 2.0. The original project implements\n55: techniques described by Howard Chen and Can Akay; their credits are retained.\n56: \n57: DeepPi's additions are its exact direct-V4 boundary, measured Pi cache/cost\n58: telemetry, prefix-churn diagnostics, batch-aware retry guards, atomic hashline\n59: edits, removal of destructive rewind behavior, and tests against current Pi\n60: event shapes.\n\n(End of file - total 60 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# DeepPi\n\nReasonix-style DeepSeek price/performance for the Pi coding agent.\n\nDeepPi targets the direct DeepSeek API only. It stabilizes cacheable request\nprefixes, reports measured cache economics from Pi's real usage records, and\nreduces paid retries with loop guards and hash-verified edits.\n\n## Supported models\n\n- `deepseek-v4-flash`\n- `deepseek-v4-pro`\n\nDeepPi is dormant for every other provider and model.\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\npi install git:github.com/christopherarter/deep-pi\n```","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.pi/extensions/deep-pi/README.md","text":"# DeepPi\n\nReasonix-style DeepSeek price/performance for the Pi coding agent.\n\nDeepPi targets the direct DeepSeek API only. It stabilizes cacheable request\nprefixes, reports measured cache economics from Pi's real usage records, and\nreduces paid retries with loop guards and hash-verified edits.\n\n## Supported models\n\n- `deepseek-v4-flash`\n- `deepseek-v4-pro`\n\nDeepPi is dormant for every other provider and model.\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\npi install git:github.com/christopherarter/deep-pi\n```\n\nReload Pi, select a supported direct DeepSeek model, and run `/deeppi`.\n\n## What `/deeppi` measures\n\n- cache-read and uncached input tokens;\n- cache-hit rate;\n- actual input cost from Pi;\n- estimated savings against fully uncached input;\n- detected local prefix churn;\n- guarded retry loops and hashline edit outcomes.\n\nDeepPi does not promise a fixed hit rate. Provider cache expiry and backend\nstate can produce misses even when the local request prefix is stable.\n\n## Development\n\n```bash\nnpm install --ignore-scripts\nnpm run verify\n```\n\nDefault verification never calls an external API. The paid smoke benchmark is\nexplicitly opt-in:\n\n```bash\nDEEPPI_LIVE=1 npm run benchmark:live\n```\n\n## Attribution\n\nDeepPi is derived from\n[`jrimmer/pi-deepseek-optimized`](https://github.com/jrimmer/pi-deepseek-optimized)\nand is licensed under the Apache License 2.0. The original project implements\ntechniques described by Howard Chen and Can Akay; their credits are retained.\n\nDeepPi's additions are its exact direct-V4 boundary, measured Pi cache/cost\ntelemetry, prefix-churn diagnostics, batch-aware retry guards, atomic hashline\nedits, removal of destructive rewind behavior, and tests against current Pi\nevent shapes.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":60,"totalLines":60,"truncated":false}},"title":".pi/extensions/deep-pi/README.md","time":{"start":1786167704366,"end":1786167704374}},"id":"prt_fdfe43a75001KUbRt4W43tA80o","sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","messageID":"msg_fdfe42a20001xkMbv3MJIzS2fF"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786167704707,"sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_ET_42X4iFXSJHXSuloE0EuA9865","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat \".pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json\"; echo \"=== pco package.json ===\"; cat \".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/package.json\""},"output":"{\n  \"name\": \"@arter/deep-pi\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"description\": \"Direct DeepSeek cache economics, prefix stability, and retry reduction for the Pi coding agent.\",\n  \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\",\n  \"author\": \"Christopher Arter\",\n  \"repository\": {\n    \"type\": \"git\",\n    \"url\": \"git+https://github.com/christopherarter/deep-pi.git\"\n  },\n  \"homepage\": \"https://github.com/christopherarter/deep-pi#readme\",\n  \"bugs\": {\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/christopherarter/deep-pi/issues\"\n  },\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"sideEffects\": false,\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \">=22.19.0\"\n  },\n  \"keywords\": [\n    \"pi-package\",\n    \"pi\",\n    \"deepseek\",\n    \"prompt-cache\",\n    \"cache-telemetry\",\n    \"hashline-editing\"\n  ],\n  \"pi\": {\n    \"extensions\": [\n      \"./extensions/deeppi.ts\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"publishConfig\": {\n    \"access\": \"public\"\n  },\n  \"files\": [\n    \"LICENSE\",\n    \"README.md\",\n    \"extensions\",\n    \"tsconfig.json\"\n  ],\n  \"peerDependencies\": {\n    \"@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent\": \"*\",\n    \"@earendil-works/pi-tui\": \"*\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@types/node\": \"^24.12.4\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.9.3\",\n    \"vitest\": \"^4.1.7\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"vitest --run\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"pack:dry\": \"npm pack --dry-run\",\n    \"verify\": \"npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run pack:dry\",\n    \"benchmark:live\": \"node scripts/live-benchmark.mjs\"\n  },\n  \"contributors\": [\n    \"Jason Rimmer\"\n  ]\n}\n=== pco package.json ===\n{\n  \"name\": \"pi-cache-optimizer\",\n  \"version\": \"2.8.0\",\n  \"description\": \"Improve Pi prompt/KV cache hit rates with stable prompts, OpenAI-compatible cache keys, proxy compat warnings, and footer cache stats.\",\n  \"keywords\": [\n    \"pi-package\",\n    \"deepseek\",\n    \"openai\",\n    \"claude\",\n    \"gemini\",\n    \"cache\",\n    \"kv-cache\",\n    \"prompt-cache\",\n    \"optimizer\"\n  ],\n  \"author\": \"freescheme\",\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"files\": [\n    \"index.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"pi\": {\n    \"extensions\": [\n      \"./index.ts\"\n    ],\n    \"image\": \"https://img.shields.io/badge/Pi-Cache%20Optimizer-4A90D9\"\n  },\n  \"imports\": {\n    \"#extension\": \"./index.ts\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"node --import jiti/register tests/review-findings.test.ts\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit --pretty false\",\n    \"check:diff\": \"git diff --check\",\n    \"check:pack\": \"npm pack --dry-run --cache node_modules/.cache/npm\",\n    \"check\": \"npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run check:diff && npm run check:pack\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@types/node\": \"^22.0.0\",\n    \"jiti\": \"^2.7.0\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.8.3\"\n  },\n  \"peerDependencies\": {\n    \"@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent\": \"*\"\n  },\n  \"repository\": {\n    \"type\": \"git\",\n    \"url\": \"git+https://github.com/jiangge/pi-cache-optimizer.git\"\n  }\n}\n","metadata":{"output":"{\n  \"name\": \"@arter/deep-pi\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"description\": \"Direct DeepSeek cache economics, prefix stability, and retry reduction for the Pi coding agent.\",\n  \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\",\n  \"author\": \"Christopher Arter\",\n  \"repository\": {\n    \"type\": \"git\",\n    \"url\": \"git+https://github.com/christopherarter/deep-pi.git\"\n  },\n  \"homepage\": \"https://github.com/christopherarter/deep-pi#readme\",\n  \"bugs\": {\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/christopherarter/deep-pi/issues\"\n  },\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"sideEffects\": false,\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \">=22.19.0\"\n  },\n  \"keywords\": [\n    \"pi-package\",\n    \"pi\",\n    \"deepseek\",\n    \"prompt-cache\",\n    \"cache-telemetry\",\n    \"hashline-editing\"\n  ],\n  \"pi\": {\n    \"extensions\": [\n      \"./extensions/deeppi.ts\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"publishConfig\": {\n    \"access\": \"public\"\n  },\n  \"files\": [\n    \"LICENSE\",\n    \"README.md\",\n    \"extensions\",\n    \"tsconfig.json\"\n  ],\n  \"peerDependencies\": {\n    \"@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent\": \"*\",\n    \"@earendil-works/pi-tui\": \"*\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@types/node\": \"^24.12.4\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.9.3\",\n    \"vitest\": \"^4.1.7\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"vitest --run\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"pack:dry\": \"npm pack --dry-run\",\n    \"verify\": \"npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run pack:dry\",\n    \"benchmark:live\": \"node scripts/live-benchmark.mjs\"\n  },\n  \"contributors\": [\n    \"Jason Rimmer\"\n  ]\n}\n=== pco package.json ===\n{\n  \"name\": \"pi-cache-optimizer\",\n  \"version\": \"2.8.0\",\n  \"description\": \"Improve Pi prompt/KV cache hit rates with stable prompts, OpenAI-compatible cache keys, proxy compat warnings, and footer cache stats.\",\n  \"keywords\": [\n    \"pi-package\",\n    \"deepseek\",\n    \"openai\",\n    \"claude\",\n    \"gemini\",\n    \"cache\",\n    \"kv-cache\",\n    \"prompt-cache\",\n    \"optimizer\"\n  ],\n  \"author\": \"freescheme\",\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"files\": [\n    \"index.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"pi\": {\n    \"extensions\": [\n      \"./index.ts\"\n    ],\n    \"image\": \"https://img.shields.io/badge/Pi-Cache%20Optimizer-4A90D9\"\n  },\n  \"imports\": {\n    \"#extension\": \"./index.ts\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"node --import jiti/register tests/review-findings.test.ts\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit --pretty false\",\n    \"check:diff\": \"git diff --check\",\n    \"check:pack\": \"npm pack --dry-run --cache node_modules/.cache/npm\",\n    \"check\": \"npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run check:diff && npm run check:pack\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@types/node\": \"^22.0.0\",\n    \"jiti\": \"^2.7.0\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.8.3\"\n  },\n  \"peerDependencies\": {\n    \"@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent\": \"*\"\n  },\n  \"repository\": {\n    \"type\": \"git\",\n    \"url\": \"git+https://github.com/jiangge/pi-cache-optimizer.git\"\n  }\n}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cat \".pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json\"; echo \"=== pco package.json ===\"; cat \".pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/package.json\"","time":{"start":1786167704704,"end":1786167704706}},"id":"prt_fdfe43b5b001gNbSvbyHOZQL3X","sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","messageID":"msg_fdfe42a20001xkMbv3MJIzS2fF"}}
