{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1786168061779,"sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","part":{"id":"prt_fdfe9af51001HOAI2leQ20z1do","messageID":"msg_fdfe9a317001MVgyusqZFOPLaO","sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786168065983,"sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_GqQZIax0eIO7usJLxXyp2970","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/research.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/research.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Research Synthesis: Improving the Packet 039 Pi Forks\n2: \n3: ## 1. Executive Summary\n4: \n5: The next improvement cycle should begin with executable evidence, then fix `pi-cache-optimizer` persistence correctness, then give DeepPi a versioned persistent report. Those three packages unlock reliable cold-start characterization, credential-independent routing checks, and honest cost comparisons without first expanding either fork's architecture.\n6: \n7: The strongest demonstrated defect is `pi-cache-optimizer`'s shared statistics transaction. Its per-process serializer does not protect concurrent processes, and a malformed file is silently treated as empty before the next write. Atomic rename prevents a partial file but not lost updates or destruction of corrupt evidence. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4215] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4264] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4293]\n8: \n9: DeepPi's largest operational gap is observability rather than its guarded routing. The full report is coupled to `ctx.ui.notify`, no cross-session stats file exists, and the documented live benchmark points to a missing script. A pure structured report feeding both TUI rendering and an atomic numeric snapshot closes all three evidence gaps cleanly. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts:64] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json:56]\n10: \n11: ## 2. Research Question and Scope\n12: \n13: This lineage evaluated both packet 039 forks for concrete improvements in correctness, test coverage, telemetry, cost economics, and maintainability. It treated four known limitations as starting facts: incomplete non-interactive DeepPi reports, no persistent DeepPi statistics, an unresolved credential-blocked live check, and uncharacterized cache-optimizer cold starts.\n14: \n15: The research inspected the two vendored packages, their tests and manifests, and the sibling packet evidence. It used official DeepSeek documentation for current cache semantics and mutable price data. It did not change either extension or run paid provider traffic.\n16: \n17: ## 3. Decision\n18: \n19: Use this dependency order:\n20: \n21: 1. Restore and package the DeepPi live benchmark; add a fake-provider routing matrix, a shared ownership fixture, and first/second/restart cold-start fixtures.\n22: 2. Harden `pi-cache-optimizer` persistence with cross-process serialization, corruption quarantine, exclusive unique temp files, cleanup, and fault/race tests.\n23: 3. Add a versioned DeepPi numeric snapshot generated by a pure report builder and consumed by both TUI and automation.\n24: 4. Correct cost labels and cache-write accounting, then run a repeated enabled/disabled crossover benchmark with price provenance.\n25: 5. Add fork build identities, patch ledgers, package hygiene gates, then extract cache-optimizer modules one characterized seam at a time.\n26: \n27: Defer a DeepPi cross-process edit lock until a concurrent-writer failure is reproducible. The TOCTOU window is real, but a stale-lock protocol adds complexity without current deployment evidence that it outranks the demonstrated stats-loss path. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts:83]\n28: \n29: ## 4. Current Architecture and Ownership Boundary\n30: \n31: DeepPi owns direct DeepSeek V4-style routes. `pi-cache-optimizer` contains a duplicate `isDeepPiOwned` predicate and skips all six relevant hooks for those routes. Prior live evidence already proved that guard, so further work should target contract drift rather than re-proving the broad behavior manually. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/eligibility.ts:1] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:1279] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:7280]\n32: \n33: The predicate must remain narrow. A broad “DeepSeek-like” match would incorrectly exclude proxy and future model routes that DeepPi does not actually own. A shared fixture matrix should exercise both implementations across provider, API, base URL, known ids, aliases, and unknown future ids. This gives one executable contract without a shared runtime dependency.\n34: \n35: ## 5. Correctness Findings\n36: \n37: ### Cache-optimizer persistence\n38: \n39: The stats path is an unlocked cross-process read/merge/write transaction. Two Pi processes can read the same baseline, merge different updates, and atomically rename different snapshots; the last rename wins. Use an advisory lock with bounded acquisition and stale-owner recovery, or another cross-process transaction primitive, around the complete read/merge/write sequence. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4264]\n40: \n41: Malformed state is caught and treated as empty, then may be overwritten. Quarantine the original with a timestamped name, increment a parse-failure health counter, notify once, and only then initialize a new file. Temp files should use random unique names, exclusive creation, and `finally` cleanup. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4293] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts:58]\n42: \n43: ### DeepPi edit safety\n44: \n45: DeepPi verifies expected content before atomic replacement and detects some subsequent drift, but another process can modify the target between the expected-content read and rename. This is a real compare-and-swap gap, yet no recorded live clobber establishes urgency. First add a two-writer negative control; promote lock work only if the race reproduces or deployment actually permits concurrent writers. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts:83] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts:91]\n46: \n47: ## 6. Test Coverage Strategy\n48: \n49: DeepPi's manifest and README advertise `scripts/live-benchmark.mjs`, but the file is absent and the package allowlist omits `scripts`. The existing package test only asserts the script string, so it locks in a broken contract. The replacement test must prove the referenced file exists and appears in the dry-run package. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json:36] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json:56] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/tests/package.test.ts:8]\n50: \n51: The missing OpenCode credential should not block the ownership regression. A local fake Pi/provider fixture can fire each guarded hook across owned and non-owned route cases, capture outbound request shape, and verify only the owning extension transforms it. Keep one optional credentialed smoke test for provider reality; do not make it the only boundary proof. [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/006-fork-and-improve-deep-pi/003-live-verification-and-closeout/tasks.md:60]\n52: \n53: `pi-cache-optimizer` tests concentrate on prompt output, footer rendering, compatibility parsing, JSONC handling, and the ownership guard. Add direct tests for state migration, corrupt-file quarantine, injected write failures, temp cleanup, two-process updates, adapter normalization, and end-to-end `message_end` accounting. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/tests/review-findings.test.ts] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:3645]\n54: \n55: Cold-start characterization needs three structured observations for each newly added model: first response with zero read/nonzero write or miss behavior, an identical warm response, and an identical response after a fresh process. Inspect normalized usage and persisted counters, not the footer, because cache-write display is adapter-dependent. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:2635] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:3645]\n56: \n57: ## 7. Telemetry and Observability Design\n58: \n59: Create separate versioned files per extension. Never create one shared writable store.\n60: \n61: For DeepPi, a pure report builder should produce a schema with `version`, local day, hashed session id, provider/model identity, response count, hit/miss/write tokens, actual cost, `estimatedSavingsVsNoCache`, retry/edit/error counts, health counters, price provenance, and `updatedAt`. Persist numeric and enum data only—no prompts, outputs, tool arguments, credentials, headers, raw errors, or raw session ids. The current-session view can reset independently; daily cumulative totals survive restarts. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/telemetry.ts:27] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:330]\n62: \n63: For `pi-cache-optimizer`, preserve aggregate economics and add bounded daily health totals: parse/write failures, missing usage, zero-read/nonzero-write observations, ownership skips, prompt-integrity fallbacks, and compatibility fallback activations. Its current last-50 request samples are memory-only; do not turn them into an unbounded durable event log. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:370] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:6818]\n64: \n65: Separate structured data, text rendering, and transport. Render `/deeppi report` from the same object written to disk, and provide a tiny read-only JSON report command. This avoids relying on RPC/UI forwarding and makes report tests independent of terminal behavior. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts:64]\n66: \n67: ## 8. Cost Economics\n68: \n69: DeepPi's savings arithmetic is valid as a fully uncached counterfactual when `usage.input` is the miss class and `usage.cacheRead` is the hit class. It is not a measured DeepPi treatment effect because DeepSeek caching is automatic. Rename the field to `estimatedSavingsVsNoCache`; causal language requires an extension enabled/disabled ablation. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/telemetry.ts:47] [SOURCE: https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/kv_cache]\n70: \n71: The current calculation ignores nonzero `cacheWrite` in availability, totals, and cost. Direct DeepSeek documentation exposes hit/miss accounting and no separately billed write class, so the direct route likely reports zero. Keep the normalized field, include its model-provided cost when present, and record a health warning when the assumption changes. [SOURCE: https://api-docs.deepseek.com/api/create-completion]\n72: \n73: Prices must be provenance, not constants asserted by behavior tests. Runtime computation already uses Pi model metadata; benchmark outputs should record provider/model, currency, price snapshot, and capture time. Synthetic prices remain the correct way to test arithmetic because DeepSeek's published table can change. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/telemetry.ts:61] [SOURCE: https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing?push_animated=1&show_loading=0&theme=light&webview_progress_bar=1]\n74: \n75: ## 9. Benchmark Design\n76: \n77: Use a paired randomized crossover with fixed prompt and tool fixtures. For each target model and round:\n78: \n79: 1. Randomize extension enabled/disabled order.\n80: 2. Record request 1 as cold, repeat the identical request twice as warm, and repeat after a fresh Pi process.\n81: 3. Capture normalized hit/miss/write tokens, input/output cost, provider latency, retries, request-prefix hash and byte length, model identity, price snapshot, and cache age.\n82: 4. Report distributions and paired deltas across multiple rounds; do not publish a single cold/warm percentage.\n83: \n84: DeepSeek documents automatic best-effort caching and a construction delay, so repeats and process restarts are required. [SOURCE: https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/kv_cache]\n85: \n86: Measure extension overhead separately with monotonic per-hook timing. DeepPi also needs temporary feature ablations for prompt shaping, tool-description shortening, and hashline editing; otherwise aggregate on/off results cannot identify which module caused a benefit or regression.\n87: \n88: ## 10. Maintainability and Fork Stewardship\n89: \n90: Both manifests retain upstream versions and upstream repository/issue metadata despite local changes. Add unique fork build versions, upstream base refs, local owner/contact metadata, and a machine-readable patch ledger containing patch ids, owned files, tests, last reconciliation date, and tree/patch checksum. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/package.json:3] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/package.json:45] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json:3] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json:7]\n91: \n92: DeepPi already has module boundaries but declares `HashlineStats` twice. TypeScript interface merging makes this compile, so it is a hygiene signal rather than a runtime defect. Add package-content validation, duplicate-symbol/lint checks, and source-size budgets. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts:165] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts:183]\n93: \n94: `pi-cache-optimizer` is an 8,390-line entry module with a large production `__internals_for_tests` export. After characterization tests, extract stable seams in this order: eligibility/model families, persistence/migrations, adapter normalization, prompt transforms, compatibility diagnostics, then UI/hook wiring. Preserve the public entry point through each move. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:6471]\n95: \n96: ## 11. Recommendations\n97: \n98: | Priority | Recommendation | Why now | Proof required |\n99: |---:|---|---|---|\n100: | 1 | Evidence floor: benchmark artifact, fake provider, ownership matrix, cold/warm/restart fixture | Low blast radius; unlocks every later claim | package dry-run plus deterministic routing and usage assertions |\n101: | 2 | Harden cache-optimizer persistence | Mechanically demonstrable lost-update and corrupt-overwrite risks | two-process and fault-injection tests preserve all data/evidence |\n102: | 3 | Add DeepPi structured persistent report | Closes non-interactive, persistence, and benchmark evidence gaps together | TUI and JSON share one report object; restart retains daily totals |\n103: | 4 | Correct economics semantics and run crossover | Prevents non-causal savings claims | paired deltas with price provenance and separate hook timing |\n104: | 5 | Add fork identity, patch ledger, and hygiene gates | Cheap protection against upstream/local ambiguity | manifests and checksums validate offline |\n105: | 6 | Extract cache-optimizer modules incrementally | Reduces future merge and test cost | unchanged characterization suite after every seam |\n106: | 7 | Investigate DeepPi edit locking | Plausible risk, weaker current evidence | reproducible two-writer clobber or real concurrent-writer deployment |\n107: \n108: ## Eliminated Alternatives\n109: \n110: | Approach | Reason Eliminated | Evidence | Iteration(s) |\n111: |---|---|---|---:|\n112: | Broad DeepSeek-like ownership predicate | Excludes routes DeepPi does not own and makes future ids active without a compatible state contract | duplicated narrow predicates | 1 |\n113: | Atomic rename as transaction concurrency | Prevents partial files but not cross-process lost updates | read/merge/rename transaction | 2 |\n114: | Permanent sidecar lock without stale recovery | A crash can turn correctness hardening into permanent outage | lock lifecycle analysis | 2 |\n115: | Raw test counts as coverage | Counts do not show unexecuted responsibilities or branches | responsibility-to-test mapping | 3 |\n116: | Real credentials as the only routing proof | Makes deterministic ownership checks unavailable in CI and reproduced the known block | credential-blocked task evidence | 3 |\n117: | Footer-only cold-start measurement | Cache-write visibility is adapter-dependent and omits structured state | usage/display paths | 3 |\n118: | RPC/UI notifications as canonical report transport | Full report forwarding remains unproven and UI-shaped | DeepPi command boundary | 4 |\n119: | Content-bearing telemetry | Adds privacy and retention risk without helping aggregate economics | required fields analysis | 4 |\n120: | One shared writable stats file | Couples failure domains and amplifies cross-process contention | persistence analysis | 4 |\n121: | `estimatedSavings` as extension-caused savings | Automatic provider caching invalidates causal attribution without ablation | DeepSeek cache guide | 5 |\n122: | One cold/warm request pair | Best-effort cache construction and timing variance confound the result | DeepSeek cache guide | 5 |\n123: | Hard-coded current provider prices in tests | Published rates are mutable; behavior tests should prove arithmetic | DeepSeek pricing docs | 5 |\n124: | Shared runtime eligibility module | Creates packaging and release coupling between independent extensions | package boundaries | 6 |\n125: | One-shot cache-optimizer split | Expands behavioral blast radius before characterization coverage | monolithic export surface | 6-7 |\n126: | Clean-history fork replacement | Erases the stable upstream comparison needed for reconciliation | provenance requirements | 6 |\n127: | DeepPi edit lock as first priority | No observed clobber; lock recovery could add a worse failure | compare-and-swap risk ranking | 7 |\n128: | More RPC probing before snapshots | Does not solve durable automation even if one mode forwards more text | report transport analysis | 7 |\n129: | Single composite cache-improvement percentage | Mixes provider caching, extension transforms, price changes, and local overhead | benchmark decomposition | 7 |\n130: \n131: ## Divergence Map\n132: \n133: No divergent-mode pivots, Council artifacts, pivot failures, or audited overrides were recorded. Breadth came from seven scheduled focus tracks: architecture, correctness, testing, observability, cost economics, maintainability, and adversarial prioritization. Saturated directions were RPC-first reporting, credential-only proof, single-pair cache benchmarking, shared writable telemetry, and one-shot modularization. The remaining frontier is empirical: paid crossover sample size, real multi-process failure frequency, and whether DeepPi ever runs beside external concurrent file writers.\n134: \n135: ## 12. Open Questions\n136: \n137: - What budget and target model matrix should govern paid crossover rounds?\n138: - Does Pi ever normalize a direct DeepSeek response into nonzero `cacheWrite`, and if so what cost metadata accompanies it?\n139: - Are multiple Pi processes expected to share the same cache-optimizer state path in normal deployment, or only in tests and automation?\n140: - Do real DeepPi deployments permit concurrent external writers to files being edited by `edit_lines`?\n141: \n142: These are implementation/operations inputs. None blocks the proposed evidence and persistence foundation.\n143: \n144: ## 13. Known-Limitation Advancement\n145: \n146: | Starting limitation | Advancement from this research |\n147: |---|---|\n148: | Full DeepPi report unavailable non-interactively | Use a versioned atomic numeric snapshot generated by the same pure report object as TUI output |\n149: | DeepPi lacks persistent stats | Add session plus daily cumulative scopes with privacy-bounded schema and health counters |\n150: | OpenCode credential blocked a live regression | Prove routing locally with a fake-provider matrix; retain credentialed smoke as optional confirmation |\n151: | Cache-optimizer cold-start writes uncharacterized | Execute structured first/second/restart fixtures across newly added models, independent of footer display |\n152: \n153: ## 14. Testable Acceptance Conditions\n154: \n155: - Two cache-optimizer processes updating the same baseline preserve both increments across repeated race runs.\n156: - A malformed stats file is quarantined byte-for-byte and never silently overwritten.\n157: - Injected write/rename failures leave no orphan temp files and preserve the last valid snapshot.\n158: - Every ownership fixture returns the same result from both forks, and only one extension transforms each route.\n159: - `npm pack --dry-run` includes every documented benchmark executable.\n160: - DeepPi TUI text and JSON snapshot are generated from an identical structured report object.\n161: - Restarted DeepPi sessions retain daily totals but reset session counters by documented semantics.\n162: - Cold/warm/restart fixtures record normalized hit/miss/write classes for every newly added model.\n163: - Benchmark output labels no-cache counterfactual savings separately from enabled/disabled treatment delta.\n164: - Every benchmark result records price provenance and local hook duration separately from provider latency.\n165: \n166: ## 15. Implementation Boundaries\n167: \n168: Keep the state files separate and versioned. Avoid prompt/output persistence. Do not widen DeepPi ownership while adding telemetry. Preserve the cache optimizer's default export and existing behavior during extraction. Add dependencies only if Node/Git primitives cannot provide bounded cross-process locking with stale recovery. Treat live provider calls as an explicit-cost optional suite.\n169: \n170: ## 16. Trade-offs, Risks, and Convergence Report\n171: \n172: The evidence-first order delays the attractive monolith cleanup, but lowers the chance of moving defects across modules without noticing. File snapshots add disk I/O; batching and serialized writers should keep it bounded. Cross-process locks improve state correctness but need timeouts and stale-owner recovery. Feature ablations improve causal inference but should remain benchmark controls rather than permanent user complexity unless they prove operational value.\n173: \n174: ### Convergence Report\n175: \n176: - Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached`\n177: - Total iterations: 7\n178: - Questions answered: 5 / 5\n179: - Remaining tracked questions: 0\n180: - Last three iteration ratios: 0.85 → 0.75 → 0.45\n181: - Convergence threshold: 0.05\n182: - Policy result: threshold was telemetry only before iteration 7; the loop stopped at the configured maximum.\n183: - Divergence summary: no divergence registry events; review breadth was achieved by explicit focus rotation.\n184: \n185: ## 17. References\n186: \n187: ### Local primary evidence\n188: \n189: - `.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts`\n190: - `.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/tests/review-findings.test.ts`\n191: - `.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/package.json`\n192: - `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts`\n193: - `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/eligibility.ts`\n194: - `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/telemetry.ts`\n195: - `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts`\n196: - `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/tests/package.test.ts`\n197: - `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json`\n198: - sibling packet 039 specifications and closeout evidence\n199: \n200: ### External primary evidence\n201: \n202: - DeepSeek, [Context Caching](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/kv_cache)\n203: - DeepSeek, [Completion API usage accounting](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/api/create-completion)\n204: - DeepSeek, [Current pricing](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing?push_animated=1&show_loading=0&theme=light&webview_progress_bar=1)\n\n(End of file - total 204 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Research Synthesis: Improving the Packet 039 Pi Forks\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nThe next improvement cycle should begin with executable evidence, then fix `pi-cache-optimizer` persistence correctness, then give DeepPi a versioned persistent report. Those three packages unlock reliable cold-start characterization, credential-independent routing checks, and honest cost comparisons without first expanding either fork's architecture.\n\nThe strongest demonstrated defect is `pi-cache-optimizer`'s shared statistics transaction. Its per-process serializer does not protect concurrent processes, and a malformed file is silently treated as empty before the next write. Atomic rename prevents a partial file but not lost updates or destruction of corrupt evidence. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4215] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4264] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4293]\n\nDeepPi's largest operational gap is observability rather than its guarded routing. The full report is coupled to `ctx.ui.notify`, no cross-session stats file exists, and the documented live benchmark points to a missing script. A pure structured report feeding both TUI rendering and an atomic numeric snapshot closes all three evidence gaps cleanly. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts:64] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json:56]\n\n## 2. Research Question and Scope\n\nThis lineage evaluated both packet 039 forks for concrete improvements in correctness, test coverage, telemetry, cost economics, and maintainability. It treated four known limitations as starting facts: incomplete non-interactive DeepPi reports, no persistent DeepPi statistics, an unresolved credential-blocked live check, and uncharacterized cache-optimizer cold starts.\n\nThe research inspected the two vendored packages, their tests and manifests, and the sibling packet evidence. It used official DeepSeek documentation for current cache semantics and mutable price data. It did not change either extension or run paid provider traffic.\n\n## 3. Decision\n\nUse this dependency order:\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/research.md","text":"# Research Synthesis: Improving the Packet 039 Pi Forks\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nThe next improvement cycle should begin with executable evidence, then fix `pi-cache-optimizer` persistence correctness, then give DeepPi a versioned persistent report. Those three packages unlock reliable cold-start characterization, credential-independent routing checks, and honest cost comparisons without first expanding either fork's architecture.\n\nThe strongest demonstrated defect is `pi-cache-optimizer`'s shared statistics transaction. Its per-process serializer does not protect concurrent processes, and a malformed file is silently treated as empty before the next write. Atomic rename prevents a partial file but not lost updates or destruction of corrupt evidence. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4215] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4264] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4293]\n\nDeepPi's largest operational gap is observability rather than its guarded routing. The full report is coupled to `ctx.ui.notify`, no cross-session stats file exists, and the documented live benchmark points to a missing script. A pure structured report feeding both TUI rendering and an atomic numeric snapshot closes all three evidence gaps cleanly. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts:64] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json:56]\n\n## 2. Research Question and Scope\n\nThis lineage evaluated both packet 039 forks for concrete improvements in correctness, test coverage, telemetry, cost economics, and maintainability. It treated four known limitations as starting facts: incomplete non-interactive DeepPi reports, no persistent DeepPi statistics, an unresolved credential-blocked live check, and uncharacterized cache-optimizer cold starts.\n\nThe research inspected the two vendored packages, their tests and manifests, and the sibling packet evidence. It used official DeepSeek documentation for current cache semantics and mutable price data. It did not change either extension or run paid provider traffic.\n\n## 3. Decision\n\nUse this dependency order:\n\n1. Restore and package the DeepPi live benchmark; add a fake-provider routing matrix, a shared ownership fixture, and first/second/restart cold-start fixtures.\n2. Harden `pi-cache-optimizer` persistence with cross-process serialization, corruption quarantine, exclusive unique temp files, cleanup, and fault/race tests.\n3. Add a versioned DeepPi numeric snapshot generated by a pure report builder and consumed by both TUI and automation.\n4. Correct cost labels and cache-write accounting, then run a repeated enabled/disabled crossover benchmark with price provenance.\n5. Add fork build identities, patch ledgers, package hygiene gates, then extract cache-optimizer modules one characterized seam at a time.\n\nDefer a DeepPi cross-process edit lock until a concurrent-writer failure is reproducible. The TOCTOU window is real, but a stale-lock protocol adds complexity without current deployment evidence that it outranks the demonstrated stats-loss path. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts:83]\n\n## 4. Current Architecture and Ownership Boundary\n\nDeepPi owns direct DeepSeek V4-style routes. `pi-cache-optimizer` contains a duplicate `isDeepPiOwned` predicate and skips all six relevant hooks for those routes. Prior live evidence already proved that guard, so further work should target contract drift rather than re-proving the broad behavior manually. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/eligibility.ts:1] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:1279] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:7280]\n\nThe predicate must remain narrow. A broad “DeepSeek-like” match would incorrectly exclude proxy and future model routes that DeepPi does not actually own. A shared fixture matrix should exercise both implementations across provider, API, base URL, known ids, aliases, and unknown future ids. This gives one executable contract without a shared runtime dependency.\n\n## 5. Correctness Findings\n\n### Cache-optimizer persistence\n\nThe stats path is an unlocked cross-process read/merge/write transaction. Two Pi processes can read the same baseline, merge different updates, and atomically rename different snapshots; the last rename wins. Use an advisory lock with bounded acquisition and stale-owner recovery, or another cross-process transaction primitive, around the complete read/merge/write sequence. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4264]\n\nMalformed state is caught and treated as empty, then may be overwritten. Quarantine the original with a timestamped name, increment a parse-failure health counter, notify once, and only then initialize a new file. Temp files should use random unique names, exclusive creation, and `finally` cleanup. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:4293] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts:58]\n\n### DeepPi edit safety\n\nDeepPi verifies expected content before atomic replacement and detects some subsequent drift, but another process can modify the target between the expected-content read and rename. This is a real compare-and-swap gap, yet no recorded live clobber establishes urgency. First add a two-writer negative control; promote lock work only if the race reproduces or deployment actually permits concurrent writers. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts:83] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts:91]\n\n## 6. Test Coverage Strategy\n\nDeepPi's manifest and README advertise `scripts/live-benchmark.mjs`, but the file is absent and the package allowlist omits `scripts`. The existing package test only asserts the script string, so it locks in a broken contract. The replacement test must prove the referenced file exists and appears in the dry-run package. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json:36] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json:56] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/tests/package.test.ts:8]\n\nThe missing OpenCode credential should not block the ownership regression. A local fake Pi/provider fixture can fire each guarded hook across owned and non-owned route cases, capture outbound request shape, and verify only the owning extension transforms it. Keep one optional credentialed smoke test for provider reality; do not make it the only boundary proof. [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/006-fork-and-improve-deep-pi/003-live-verification-and-closeout/tasks.md:60]\n\n`pi-cache-optimizer` tests concentrate on prompt output, footer rendering, compatibility parsing, JSONC handling, and the ownership guard. Add direct tests for state migration, corrupt-file quarantine, injected write failures, temp cleanup, two-process updates, adapter normalization, and end-to-end `message_end` accounting. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/tests/review-findings.test.ts] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:3645]\n\nCold-start characterization needs three structured observations for each newly added model: first response with zero read/nonzero write or miss behavior, an identical warm response, and an identical response after a fresh process. Inspect normalized usage and persisted counters, not the footer, because cache-write display is adapter-dependent. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:2635] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:3645]\n\n## 7. Telemetry and Observability Design\n\nCreate separate versioned files per extension. Never create one shared writable store.\n\nFor DeepPi, a pure report builder should produce a schema with `version`, local day, hashed session id, provider/model identity, response count, hit/miss/write tokens, actual cost, `estimatedSavingsVsNoCache`, retry/edit/error counts, health counters, price provenance, and `updatedAt`. Persist numeric and enum data only—no prompts, outputs, tool arguments, credentials, headers, raw errors, or raw session ids. The current-session view can reset independently; daily cumulative totals survive restarts. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/telemetry.ts:27] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:330]\n\nFor `pi-cache-optimizer`, preserve aggregate economics and add bounded daily health totals: parse/write failures, missing usage, zero-read/nonzero-write observations, ownership skips, prompt-integrity fallbacks, and compatibility fallback activations. Its current last-50 request samples are memory-only; do not turn them into an unbounded durable event log. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:370] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:6818]\n\nSeparate structured data, text rendering, and transport. Render `/deeppi report` from the same object written to disk, and provide a tiny read-only JSON report command. This avoids relying on RPC/UI forwarding and makes report tests independent of terminal behavior. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts:64]\n\n## 8. Cost Economics\n\nDeepPi's savings arithmetic is valid as a fully uncached counterfactual when `usage.input` is the miss class and `usage.cacheRead` is the hit class. It is not a measured DeepPi treatment effect because DeepSeek caching is automatic. Rename the field to `estimatedSavingsVsNoCache`; causal language requires an extension enabled/disabled ablation. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/telemetry.ts:47] [SOURCE: https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/kv_cache]\n\nThe current calculation ignores nonzero `cacheWrite` in availability, totals, and cost. Direct DeepSeek documentation exposes hit/miss accounting and no separately billed write class, so the direct route likely reports zero. Keep the normalized field, include its model-provided cost when present, and record a health warning when the assumption changes. [SOURCE: https://api-docs.deepseek.com/api/create-completion]\n\nPrices must be provenance, not constants asserted by behavior tests. Runtime computation already uses Pi model metadata; benchmark outputs should record provider/model, currency, price snapshot, and capture time. Synthetic prices remain the correct way to test arithmetic because DeepSeek's published table can change. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/telemetry.ts:61] [SOURCE: https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing?push_animated=1&show_loading=0&theme=light&webview_progress_bar=1]\n\n## 9. Benchmark Design\n\nUse a paired randomized crossover with fixed prompt and tool fixtures. For each target model and round:\n\n1. Randomize extension enabled/disabled order.\n2. Record request 1 as cold, repeat the identical request twice as warm, and repeat after a fresh Pi process.\n3. Capture normalized hit/miss/write tokens, input/output cost, provider latency, retries, request-prefix hash and byte length, model identity, price snapshot, and cache age.\n4. Report distributions and paired deltas across multiple rounds; do not publish a single cold/warm percentage.\n\nDeepSeek documents automatic best-effort caching and a construction delay, so repeats and process restarts are required. [SOURCE: https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/kv_cache]\n\nMeasure extension overhead separately with monotonic per-hook timing. DeepPi also needs temporary feature ablations for prompt shaping, tool-description shortening, and hashline editing; otherwise aggregate on/off results cannot identify which module caused a benefit or regression.\n\n## 10. Maintainability and Fork Stewardship\n\nBoth manifests retain upstream versions and upstream repository/issue metadata despite local changes. Add unique fork build versions, upstream base refs, local owner/contact metadata, and a machine-readable patch ledger containing patch ids, owned files, tests, last reconciliation date, and tree/patch checksum. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/package.json:3] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/package.json:45] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json:3] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json:7]\n\nDeepPi already has module boundaries but declares `HashlineStats` twice. TypeScript interface merging makes this compile, so it is a hygiene signal rather than a runtime defect. Add package-content validation, duplicate-symbol/lint checks, and source-size budgets. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts:165] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts:183]\n\n`pi-cache-optimizer` is an 8,390-line entry module with a large production `__internals_for_tests` export. After characterization tests, extract stable seams in this order: eligibility/model families, persistence/migrations, adapter normalization, prompt transforms, compatibility diagnostics, then UI/hook wiring. Preserve the public entry point through each move. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:6471]\n\n## 11. Recommendations\n\n| Priority | Recommendation | Why now | Proof required |\n|---:|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Evidence floor: benchmark artifact, fake provider, ownership matrix, cold/warm/restart fixture | Low blast radius; unlocks every later claim | package dry-run plus deterministic routing and usage assertions |\n| 2 | Harden cache-optimizer persistence | Mechanically demonstrable lost-update and corrupt-overwrite risks | two-process and fault-injection tests preserve all data/evidence |\n| 3 | Add DeepPi structured persistent report | Closes non-interactive, persistence, and benchmark evidence gaps together | TUI and JSON share one report object; restart retains daily totals |\n| 4 | Correct economics semantics and run crossover | Prevents non-causal savings claims | paired deltas with price provenance and separate hook timing |\n| 5 | Add fork identity, patch ledger, and hygiene gates | Cheap protection against upstream/local ambiguity | manifests and checksums validate offline |\n| 6 | Extract cache-optimizer modules incrementally | Reduces future merge and test cost | unchanged characterization suite after every seam |\n| 7 | Investigate DeepPi edit locking | Plausible risk, weaker current evidence | reproducible two-writer clobber or real concurrent-writer deployment |\n\n## Eliminated Alternatives\n\n| Approach | Reason Eliminated | Evidence | Iteration(s) |\n|---|---|---|---:|\n| Broad DeepSeek-like ownership predicate | Excludes routes DeepPi does not own and makes future ids active without a compatible state contract | duplicated narrow predicates | 1 |\n| Atomic rename as transaction concurrency | Prevents partial files but not cross-process lost updates | read/merge/rename transaction | 2 |\n| Permanent sidecar lock without stale recovery | A crash can turn correctness hardening into permanent outage | lock lifecycle analysis | 2 |\n| Raw test counts as coverage | Counts do not show unexecuted responsibilities or branches | responsibility-to-test mapping | 3 |\n| Real credentials as the only routing proof | Makes deterministic ownership checks unavailable in CI and reproduced the known block | credential-blocked task evidence | 3 |\n| Footer-only cold-start measurement | Cache-write visibility is adapter-dependent and omits structured state | usage/display paths | 3 |\n| RPC/UI notifications as canonical report transport | Full report forwarding remains unproven and UI-shaped | DeepPi command boundary | 4 |\n| Content-bearing telemetry | Adds privacy and retention risk without helping aggregate economics | required fields analysis | 4 |\n| One shared writable stats file | Couples failure domains and amplifies cross-process contention | persistence analysis | 4 |\n| `estimatedSavings` as extension-caused savings | Automatic provider caching invalidates causal attribution without ablation | DeepSeek cache guide | 5 |\n| One cold/warm request pair | Best-effort cache construction and timing variance confound the result | DeepSeek cache guide | 5 |\n| Hard-coded current provider prices in tests | Published rates are mutable; behavior tests should prove arithmetic | DeepSeek pricing docs | 5 |\n| Shared runtime eligibility module | Creates packaging and release coupling between independent extensions | package boundaries | 6 |\n| One-shot cache-optimizer split | Expands behavioral blast radius before characterization coverage | monolithic export surface | 6-7 |\n| Clean-history fork replacement | Erases the stable upstream comparison needed for reconciliation | provenance requirements | 6 |\n| DeepPi edit lock as first priority | No observed clobber; lock recovery could add a worse failure | compare-and-swap risk ranking | 7 |\n| More RPC probing before snapshots | Does not solve durable automation even if one mode forwards more text | report transport analysis | 7 |\n| Single composite cache-improvement percentage | Mixes provider caching, extension transforms, price changes, and local overhead | benchmark decomposition | 7 |\n\n## Divergence Map\n\nNo divergent-mode pivots, Council artifacts, pivot failures, or audited overrides were recorded. Breadth came from seven scheduled focus tracks: architecture, correctness, testing, observability, cost economics, maintainability, and adversarial prioritization. Saturated directions were RPC-first reporting, credential-only proof, single-pair cache benchmarking, shared writable telemetry, and one-shot modularization. The remaining frontier is empirical: paid crossover sample size, real multi-process failure frequency, and whether DeepPi ever runs beside external concurrent file writers.\n\n## 12. Open Questions\n\n- What budget and target model matrix should govern paid crossover rounds?\n- Does Pi ever normalize a direct DeepSeek response into nonzero `cacheWrite`, and if so what cost metadata accompanies it?\n- Are multiple Pi processes expected to share the same cache-optimizer state path in normal deployment, or only in tests and automation?\n- Do real DeepPi deployments permit concurrent external writers to files being edited by `edit_lines`?\n\nThese are implementation/operations inputs. None blocks the proposed evidence and persistence foundation.\n\n## 13. Known-Limitation Advancement\n\n| Starting limitation | Advancement from this research |\n|---|---|\n| Full DeepPi report unavailable non-interactively | Use a versioned atomic numeric snapshot generated by the same pure report object as TUI output |\n| DeepPi lacks persistent stats | Add session plus daily cumulative scopes with privacy-bounded schema and health counters |\n| OpenCode credential blocked a live regression | Prove routing locally with a fake-provider matrix; retain credentialed smoke as optional confirmation |\n| Cache-optimizer cold-start writes uncharacterized | Execute structured first/second/restart fixtures across newly added models, independent of footer display |\n\n## 14. Testable Acceptance Conditions\n\n- Two cache-optimizer processes updating the same baseline preserve both increments across repeated race runs.\n- A malformed stats file is quarantined byte-for-byte and never silently overwritten.\n- Injected write/rename failures leave no orphan temp files and preserve the last valid snapshot.\n- Every ownership fixture returns the same result from both forks, and only one extension transforms each route.\n- `npm pack --dry-run` includes every documented benchmark executable.\n- DeepPi TUI text and JSON snapshot are generated from an identical structured report object.\n- Restarted DeepPi sessions retain daily totals but reset session counters by documented semantics.\n- Cold/warm/restart fixtures record normalized hit/miss/write classes for every newly added model.\n- Benchmark output labels no-cache counterfactual savings separately from enabled/disabled treatment delta.\n- Every benchmark result records price provenance and local hook duration separately from provider latency.\n\n## 15. Implementation Boundaries\n\nKeep the state files separate and versioned. Avoid prompt/output persistence. Do not widen DeepPi ownership while adding telemetry. Preserve the cache optimizer's default export and existing behavior during extraction. Add dependencies only if Node/Git primitives cannot provide bounded cross-process locking with stale recovery. Treat live provider calls as an explicit-cost optional suite.\n\n## 16. Trade-offs, Risks, and Convergence Report\n\nThe evidence-first order delays the attractive monolith cleanup, but lowers the chance of moving defects across modules without noticing. File snapshots add disk I/O; batching and serialized writers should keep it bounded. Cross-process locks improve state correctness but need timeouts and stale-owner recovery. Feature ablations improve causal inference but should remain benchmark controls rather than permanent user complexity unless they prove operational value.\n\n### Convergence Report\n\n- Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached`\n- Total iterations: 7\n- Questions answered: 5 / 5\n- Remaining tracked questions: 0\n- Last three iteration ratios: 0.85 → 0.75 → 0.45\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Policy result: threshold was telemetry only before iteration 7; the loop stopped at the configured maximum.\n- Divergence summary: no divergence registry events; review breadth was achieved by explicit focus rotation.\n\n## 17. References\n\n### Local primary evidence\n\n- `.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts`\n- `.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/tests/review-findings.test.ts`\n- `.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/package.json`\n- `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts`\n- `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/eligibility.ts`\n- `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/telemetry.ts`\n- `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts`\n- `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/tests/package.test.ts`\n- `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/package.json`\n- sibling packet 039 specifications and closeout evidence\n\n### External primary evidence\n\n- DeepSeek, [Context Caching](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/kv_cache)\n- DeepSeek, [Completion API usage accounting](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/api/create-completion)\n- DeepSeek, [Current pricing](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing?push_animated=1&show_loading=0&theme=light&webview_progress_bar=1)","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":204,"totalLines":204,"truncated":false}},"title":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/research.md","time":{"start":1786168065974,"end":1786168065980}},"id":"prt_fdfe9be54001fskm6BcY94J5R3","sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","messageID":"msg_fdfe9a317001MVgyusqZFOPLaO"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786168066874,"sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_Lx4K5cqVTYkXkFVjLi0e3269","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"=== sol resource-map ===\"; head -30 \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/resource-map.md\"; echo \"=== sol log ===\"; wc -l \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/logs/fanout-lineage.out\"; echo \"=== luna convergence-report.md ===\"; head -40 \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/luna/convergence-report.md\" 2>/dev/null"},"output":"=== sol resource-map ===\n---\ntitle: \"Resource Map — Packet 039 Pi Fork Improvements\"\ndescription: \"Evidence inventory for the sol detached research lineage.\"\n---\n\n# Resource Map\n\n## Summary\n\n- Local source files: 10 primary implementation/manifest/test surfaces\n- Sibling packet evidence: 3 packet branches\n- External primary sources: 3 official DeepSeek pages\n- Iteration narratives: 7\n- Scope: correctness, tests, observability, economics, and maintainability for both packet 039 forks\n\n## Implementation Sources\n\n| Resource | Category | Research use | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts` | Source | ownership guard, adapters, usage, persistence, telemetry, hook wiring, test exports | Analyzed |\n| `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts` | Source | command/report transport and module registration | Analyzed |\n| `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/eligibility.ts` | Source | canonical DeepPi ownership predicate | Analyzed |\n| `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/telemetry.ts` | Source | cost formula, session report, errors | Analyzed |\n| `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts` | Source | atomic writes, compare-and-swap boundary, duplicate interface | Analyzed |\n\n## Test and Packaging Sources\n\n| Resource | Category | Research use | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/tests/review-findings.test.ts` | Test | present coverage and missing runtime boundaries | Analyzed |\n=== sol log ===\n       1 specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/logs/fanout-lineage.out\n=== luna convergence-report.md ===\n# Convergence Report — Luna Lineage\n\n- Stop policy: `max-iterations`\n- Iterations completed: 7/7\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Novelty ratios: 0.95 → 0.84 → 0.78 → 0.68 → 0.57 → 0.43 → 0.29\n- Convergence telemetry: 0.6486\n- Early synthesis: no\n- Max-iterations reached: yes\n- Findings: 28\n- Open research questions: 0\n\nThe ratios declined as the review moved from architecture and correctness into coverage, observability, economics, maintainability, and evidence reconciliation. This did not terminate the loop early because the configured stop policy required all seven iterations. The final synthesis is in `research.md`.\n","metadata":{"output":"=== sol resource-map ===\n---\ntitle: \"Resource Map — Packet 039 Pi Fork Improvements\"\ndescription: \"Evidence inventory for the sol detached research lineage.\"\n---\n\n# Resource Map\n\n## Summary\n\n- Local source files: 10 primary implementation/manifest/test surfaces\n- Sibling packet evidence: 3 packet branches\n- External primary sources: 3 official DeepSeek pages\n- Iteration narratives: 7\n- Scope: correctness, tests, observability, economics, and maintainability for both packet 039 forks\n\n## Implementation Sources\n\n| Resource | Category | Research use | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts` | Source | ownership guard, adapters, usage, persistence, telemetry, hook wiring, test exports | Analyzed |\n| `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi.ts` | Source | command/report transport and module registration | Analyzed |\n| `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/eligibility.ts` | Source | canonical DeepPi ownership predicate | Analyzed |\n| `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/telemetry.ts` | Source | cost formula, session report, errors | Analyzed |\n| `.pi/extensions/deep-pi/extensions/deeppi/hashlines.ts` | Source | atomic writes, compare-and-swap boundary, duplicate interface | Analyzed |\n\n## Test and Packaging Sources\n\n| Resource | Category | Research use | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/tests/review-findings.test.ts` | Test | present coverage and missing runtime boundaries | Analyzed |\n=== sol log ===\n       1 specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/logs/fanout-lineage.out\n=== luna convergence-report.md ===\n# Convergence Report — Luna Lineage\n\n- Stop policy: `max-iterations`\n- Iterations completed: 7/7\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Novelty ratios: 0.95 → 0.84 → 0.78 → 0.68 → 0.57 → 0.43 → 0.29\n- Convergence telemetry: 0.6486\n- Early synthesis: no\n- Max-iterations reached: yes\n- Findings: 28\n- Open research questions: 0\n\nThe ratios declined as the review moved from architecture and correctness into coverage, observability, economics, maintainability, and evidence reconciliation. This did not terminate the loop early because the configured stop policy required all seven iterations. The final synthesis is in `research.md`.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"echo \"=== sol resource-map ===\"; head -30 \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/resource-map.md\"; echo \"=== sol log ===\"; wc -l \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/sol/logs/fanout-lineage.out\"; echo \"=== luna convergence-report.md ===\"; head -40 \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/007-research-fork-improvements/research/lineages/luna/convergence-report.md\" 2>/dev/null","time":{"start":1786168066870,"end":1786168066873}},"id":"prt_fdfe9bfde001Q1O2ygzoDxg4W5","sessionID":"ses_020238d7affe3gDc79EXqntLlP","messageID":"msg_fdfe9a317001MVgyusqZFOPLaO"}}
